# POLLY, backup and restore over USB (tools/polly_backup.py; the device's side, a cut cable, a power cut and the
# question: tests/backup_test.c): a backup of a known set; the set changed (by hand and in the flash); the backup
# put back as the device does once SEL answers RESTORE FROM USB?: everything as it was, at once and after a
# reboot. Refused while playing (STOP FIRST) and when the file is damaged: nothing changes.
wait 200
poke_pattern
reboot
expect tempo 100
expect pat1_nev 3
expect loop_ch9_0 918
backup out:polly.plb
# ---- changed: the tempo by hand (saved by the autosave), a pattern and the songs in the flash
tap HOME
spin K2 5
expect tempo 105
wait 5000
expect song0_tempo 105
poke_bad_pattern
reboot
expect pat1_nev 0
expect tempo 105
# ---- refused while playing: nothing changes
tap PLAY
wait 300
restore out:polly.plb
expect restore_rc 10
wait 200
shot stop_first.png
expect tempo 105
tap PLAY
wait 500
# ---- a damaged backup: refused, nothing changes
backup out:other.plb
backup_damage out:other.plb
restore out:other.plb
expect restore_rc 5
expect pat1_nev 0
# ---- put back: as backed up, at once (reloaded) and after a reboot
restore out:polly.plb
expect restore_rc 0
expect tempo 100
expect song0_tempo 100
expect loop_ch9_0 918
expect pat1_nev 3
wait 200
shot restored.png
reboot
expect tempo 100
expect pat1_nev 3
expect loop_ch9_0 918
